{{!
  Controller slice test: @WebMvcTest on the one controller (Spring Boot 4 package
  org.springframework.boot.webmvc.test.autoconfigure) with the
  context limited to the controller and the beans it needs (its mappers), use cases as @MockitoBean, Mothers as
  use-case results. Listing the classes, rather than scanning the controller package, keeps one controller test
  independent of the other controllers in the module.
  Exemplars: vaccination-adapter src/test .../controller/VaccinationControllerTest.java,
             authentication-adapter src/test .../controller/OAuthAdminControllerTest.java
  Target: <capability>-adapter/src/test/java/<pkg>/adapter/controller/<Name>ControllerTest.java
  Package: "package" is the full package of the file (no suffix is appended).
  Vars:   package, Name, beans[] (simple names of the other real beans, e.g. GadgetDomainToDTOMapper),
          imports[] (use cases, Mothers),
          useCases[type, field],
          cases[test (method name, givenX_whenY_thenZ), stub (Mockito statement; omit for none),
                request (MockMvc request builder, e.g. get("/api/vaccination").header("X-context", "PAGE")),
                status (MockMvc status matcher: isOk, isNoContent, isBadRequest, ...),
                jsonPaths[path, value (Java expression)]]
  Left to you: a JSON response fixture (getResourceAsStream) when the body is large.
}}
